From: bjakra <87858321+bjakra@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:15:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pan/kmod: add a backend for Arm's kbase kernel driver

Vendor kernels drive a Mali with Arm's own driver, kbase: a character
device (/dev/mali0), not a DRM one. This backend lets panfrost render on
such a kernel, for the job manager GPUs and the ioctl form of the kbase
interface (UK 11.x; written against r26p0 on a Mali-T720).

What the DRM drivers do in the kernel is done in the backend: sync objects
are the sequence number of a job, signaled when its completion event has
been read from the device; jobs are chained with order dependencies so they
run as submitted, and each BO remembers the last job given it, for
bo_wait and for not freeing a region under a job. BOs live in kbase's
custom VA zone, where the kernel picks the GPU address, so only a 32-bit
process is supported. Executable BOs are carved from regions the size of
the GPU's program counter range, because kbase aligns each executable
region to that.

Not there yet: dma-buf import and export, CPU-cached mappings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A7tdbX9rySEX8PF9LVaYr5
